                <pb facs="0828" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg696"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7128: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-03-01T15:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 1, 1926—3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 1—6:20
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>101. My 92, February 26, noon. American consul general, Canton, reports February
                    28, 10 a.m., that presence of destroyer no longer necessary and he has so
                    advised Navy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
